            "review_title": "Review at Red Tilapia (Michelia Hotel Nha Trang)",
            "review_text": "SharonW59\nBrisbane, Australia66 contributions\n0\nJust a bit off putting\nMar 2017 • Couples\nThe shuttle bus from our cruise shipped used this hotel as the drop-off and collection point. This made it a little easier to decide to eat at this establishment.\nI agree with the comments of a number of other people, English was not the first or second language of any of the staff that we came across.\nThe food that we ordered was tasty enough. That said, we only ordered two of the light options from the lunch menu, which we shared.\nOur disappointment came with the drink order. I saw fresh watermelon juice on the menu and thought that this would be a nice cooling option to have with lunch. But then I forgot to order the drink without ice. It is a pretty good rule of thumb to order all drinks without ice. Of course, the juice arrived with ice, it was only after I had taken a sip that my husband reminded me about not having the ice. When I mentioned this to the waitress, she was a mite confused (my Vietnamese is not good and her English was not any better). Even the manager/maître de was unable to be of any assistance. In the end the waitress took away the juice, went back to the bar and simply strained the ice from the juice, we were in a direct line of sight and actually saw her do this and return the drink to the table. I was happy to pay for a new fresh juice without the ice but this is not what I got.\nJust be careful when ordering a drink, and remember - No Ice!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten April 5, 2017",
            "rating": 4.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-11",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
